    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "· Plume Fourre-Tout On Radio ·",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The undeniable showstopper was the Plume Fourre-Tout On Radio handbag. Inspired by vintage cassette radios, it reimagines the house's first leather travel bag—the Plume, born in the 1960s—in black Barénia calfskin. The bag retains its clean rectangular silhouette and generous capacity, while exquisite leather craftsmanship recreates the radio's speaker grille, tuning dials, and volume and power buttons. The cassette window opens via a button at the top, revealing a metal cardholder shaped like a cassette tape—a whimsical, artisanal touch.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
