    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A submarine-shaped bag charm pays elegant homage to the 1960s Hélice propeller cufflinks, inspired by the airship motif in French designer Loïc Dubigeon's scarf \"Les Folies du ciel.\" The leather shell is crafted using glovemaking techniques, with a propeller that spins around a lacquered saddle nail. An apple-green charm takes its cue from origami: leather is meticulously folded into a delicate paper airplane, with a closure mechanism borrowed from watch strap engineering, capable of holding cards or earphones.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
